; pacer — the SJON workspace project file.
;
; `sjon-lsp` discovers the nearest `sjon-project.sjon` at or above the file
; being edited and composes its `:plugins` into ONE ambient schema
; (`lsp/Handler.loadProject` → `Schema.init(project.plugins)`). That is what
; gives every corpus score and every example diagnostics, hover (the
; manifest's own `:description`s), form-head and key completion, and
; did-you-mean — with no `(use-plugin …)` line in the scores themselves,
; which is right: pacer PRELOADS the manifest rather than resolving it by
; name (see `src/Schema.zig`).
;
; `./schema/pacer.sjon` is the same file `build.zig` hands to `@embedFile`
; as `pacer_schema`. The two are kept honest by a test in `src/Schema.zig`
; that loads this project the way the language server does and compares its
; composed vocabulary against the preloaded one, head for head.
;
; No `:version`: same reason the manifest declares none — pacer's version
; lives in exactly three places (package.json / build.zig.zon /
; src/root.zig) and a fourth spelling would only drift.
;
; `:documents` names the files that ARE pacer scores. It scopes the `sjon`
; CLI's project-wide walk (`sjon check` with no file arguments); the
; language server does not read it — that walk is every `**/*.sjon` under
; the workspace root. Two things to know before running the CLI over this
; list: the CLI resolves a document's plugins from its own `(use-plugin …)`
; directives rather than composing the project's ambiently, so a pacer
; score — which writes none — reports `unknown_form` there; and
; `corpus/diag-*` scores are deliberately broken, their diagnostics being
; the pinned golden. `corpus/*/times.sjon` and `corpus/*/expected.sjon` are
; left out as harness / golden files in a vocabulary of their own (plan 12
; phase C2 gives them a schema); `examples/*.score.sjon` is written by
; phase D1.
(project :name pacer
  :plugins ["./schema/pacer.sjon"]
  :documents ["corpus/*/doc.sjon" "examples/*.score.sjon"])
